# Toolbox

A home for self-service utilities. The landing page is `GET /admin/toolbox` and is `@login_required` only. Individual tools apply their own permission gates:
- **Markup** (`GET /admin/toolbox/markup`) is available to every logged-in user.
- **PDF Tool** (`GET /admin/toolbox/pdf` plus `/pdf/*` API routes) stays `@admin_required`.

**Layout:** thin blueprint hub [app/toolbox/__init__.py](mdc:app/toolbox/__init__.py) (`toolbox_bp`, landing `GET /`), shared path helpers [app/toolbox/common.py](mdc:app/toolbox/common.py), Markup route [app/toolbox/markup.py](mdc:app/toolbox/markup.py), PDF Tool routes + staging [app/toolbox/pdf.py](mdc:app/toolbox/pdf.py). Processing primitives in [app/pdf_tools.py](mdc:app/pdf_tools.py) are shared with Batch PDF Import. New tools → add `app/toolbox/<tool>.py`, import it from `__init__.py` after the blueprint is created, and add a card to `templates/admin_toolbox.html`. The Toolbox is linked from the all-user **My Stuff** navbar dropdown; admin-only tools should hide their cards for non-admin users.

## Markup PWA

Standalone page [templates/markup.html](mdc:templates/markup.html), not `base.html`, to maximise drawing space. It uses Konva from CDN, `perfect-freehand` from ESM CDN, and `idb-keyval` from CDN; no build step.

PWA files:
- [app/pwa.py](mdc:app/pwa.py) serves `/manifest.webmanifest` and `/sw.js` at root scope. `/sw.js` must keep `Service-Worker-Allowed: /`.
- [static/markup/manifest.webmanifest](mdc:static/markup/manifest.webmanifest) declares the Android Web Share Target at `/admin/toolbox/markup/share-target`.
- [static/markup/sw.js](mdc:static/markup/sw.js) intercepts share-target POSTs, stores the image in Cache API, then redirects to `/admin/toolbox/markup?shared=1`.

Markup is client-side and does not save drawings server-side. Autosave is per-device IndexedDB (`oqb:markup:autosave:v1`). Export unions image/drawing bounds and writes a white-background PNG cropped to content. Present mode passes images via `?img=<same-origin-url>`; external URLs are intentionally rejected to avoid canvas-taint export failures. iOS Safari cannot register Web Share Target, so iOS relies on installed PWA + upload/paste and an optional Shortcut workflow.

## PDF Tool

## Page descriptor model (the core idea)

The working set is an ordered list of **page descriptors**, each pointing at one source-PDF page plus an ordered op chain:

```
{"id": <uuid12>, "src": <srcid>, "page": <0-based>, "ops": [ {op}, ... ], "mode": <split mode>, "mode1_pages_per_student": <int>, "dpi": <int>, "annots": [ {annot}, ... ]}
```

`dpi` is chosen per batch in step 2 (default `TOOLBOX_DEFAULT_DPI`); it is page-size independent (zoom = dpi/72), so A4 and A3 export at the same physical quality. Export uses each page's `dpi` (fallback `default_dpi`) for raster pages and as the PDF `resolution`.

Ops (applied in order by `pdf_tools.apply_ops`):
- Vector-safe: `rotate`(deg 90/180/270), `crop`(box `[x1,y1,x2,y2]` fractional 0..1, y down).
- Raster-only (`RASTER_ONLY_OPS`): `deskew`, `rotate_fine`(deg float), `brightness`/`contrast`/`sharpen`(factor), `grayscale`, `bw`(threshold 0..255).

Op order built by `build_op_chain(pre_rotate, frag_ops, filters)` = pre-rotate → split crop → image filters. `filters_to_ops` maps the UI dict `{deskew, rotate_fine, brightness, contrast, sharpen, grayscale, bw, bw_threshold}` to ops (skips no-op values).

## Annotations (redact / highlight / markup)

`annots` are separate from `ops`; coords are **fractional 0..1 of the post-ops page** (y down), so they survive rotate/crop edits only if those don't change after marking. Kinds (sanitised by `_sanitize_annots` in `app/toolbox/pdf.py`; caps: 500/page, ink ≤ 4000 pts, text ≤ 2000 chars):
- `{"id","kind":"redact","rect":[x1,y1,x2,y2],"color"}` — opaque box; truly removed on digital export.
- `{"kind":"erase","rect":[...]}` — **Remove**: like redact but always white fill (color forced `#ffffff`) — content removed, plain page left. Editor shows a dashed grey outline (`AE_ERASE_PROPS`, editor-only).
- `{"kind":"highlight","rect":[...],"color","opacity"}` — alpha overlay.
- `{"kind":"text","pos":[x,y],"text","size","color","font"}` — `size` = fraction of page height; `text` may contain newlines (drawn line-by-line at 1.2em in Konva/PIL/fitz alike); `font` ∈ `sans|serif|mono` (mapped via `pdf_tools.ANNOT_FONT_FILES` raster / `ANNOT_FONT_PDF` base-14 digital).
- `{"kind":"ink","points":[[x,y],...],"color","width","opacity"}` — freehand polyline.
- `{"kind":"image","rect":[...],"data":"data:image/(png|jpeg|webp);base64,..."}` — picture stamp (signature/logo); data-URL validated by `_DATA_URL_RE`, ≤ 4 MB b64. Raster: PIL paste with alpha; digital: `pg.insert_image(rect, rotate=pg.rotation)`.
- Optional `pending: true` = unreviewed search/AI result; rendered with a dashed orange outline, **excluded from export** until accepted.

Raster rendering: `pdf_tools.apply_annotations(img, annots)` (Pillow RGBA composite) called by `render_page_image(..., annots=)` — thumbs/previews show marks live. The Konva editor requests its background with `?annots=0`.

## Hybrid export (`pdf_tools.export_pages`)

Per page, `is_vector_safe(ops)` is true when there's no raster-only op AND not a crop+rotate combo. Vector-safe pages are cloned via `pypdf` (set `cropbox`/`mediabox` from the fractional box + `/Rotate`); a crop on a page with inherent `/Rotate` falls back to raster too. Everything else rasterises (`render_page_image(..., dpi=)` → Pillow → one-page PDF → `add_page`). Preview thumbnails ALWAYS rasterise via the same `render_page_image` but use a small fixed `width_px` (DPI is for export). `rasterize_page`/`render_page_image` accept EITHER `dpi` (export/processing) OR `width_px` (thumbnails). `pypdf` missing → all-raster PDF fallback (logged). `fmt='zip'` → ZIP of PNGs; `split_every=N` (Mode 1) → ZIP of N-page PDFs.

**Output modes** (`output=` param): `digital` (default) keeps pages vector — an annotated vector-safe page is built by `_fitz_annotated_page_bytes` (PyMuPDF: `add_redact_annot` + `apply_redactions` for both `redact` and `erase` (white fill) = content truly removed; highlights/text/ink drawn as vector overlays mapped into unrotated page space); `image` force-rasterises every page so redaction is pixel-level and unrecoverable. Pending annots are stripped by `_drop_pending_annots` before any export path.

**Size control:** after `apply_redactions` the page image of a scan is re-encoded raw — `_fitz_annotated_page_bytes` recompresses with `nd.rewrite_images(quality=85)` and saves `tobytes(deflate=True, garbage=3)` (without this a 1 MB scan ballooned to 100s of MB). **Optional compression** (`compress=` param, PDF outputs only, applied per part for split ZIPs): `{'preset': 'light'|'medium'|'strong'}` (one `rewrite_images` pass via `COMPRESS_PRESETS` — light recompress-only, medium ~150 DPI, strong ~100 DPI) or `{'target_bytes': n}` (`compress_pdf_bytes` walks `_COMPRESS_SIZE_LADDER` from the original bytes until the result fits; best effort, never larger than input).

## A3 split / reorder (`split_descriptors(num_pages, mode)`)

Half boxes `LEFT_HALF=[0,0,.5,1]` / `RIGHT_HALF=[.5,0,1,1]`. `SPLIT_MODES = ('none','simple','mode1','mode2')`; `mode1_pages_per_student` defaults to 4 and is clamped to 1..200:
- `simple`: each page → `[left, right]`.
- `mode1` (folded individual copies/booklets): use `ceil(pages_per_student/2)` A3 sides per student, order the folded booklet halves in reading order, then keep only `pages_per_student` outputs. Default 4 preserves the legacy order `p(i)_R, p(i+1)_L, p(i+1)_R, p(i)_L`; `7` keeps pages 1-7 and drops the 8th padding slot. Pair export `split_every` with the same page count for per-student ZIPs.
- `mode2` (destapled booklet): `total=2n`; for `i in range(n)`: even `i` → `ordered[total-i-1]=L_i, ordered[i]=R_i`; odd `i` → `ordered[i]=L_i, ordered[total-i-1]=R_i`. Assumes even page count.

Math ported from a standalone pypdf script; reorder happens on the rotated page (pre-rotate is applied before the crop in the op chain).

## Staging

`SYSTEM_PATH/.toolbox/<token>/` (legacy: `OUTPUT_PATH/.toolbox`) holds `session.json` (`{sources:{srcid:{filename,page_count}}, pages:[descriptor]}`) + `sources/<srcid>.pdf`. Token regex `^[0-9a-f]{8,40}$`, srcid `^[0-9a-f]{6,40}$`, validated before any join. `_cleanup_old()` (~12 h) runs on each new session. Server-PDF picks + save destinations now resolve through the unified file selector + per-user root registry via `_resolve_root_base(root_id, require_write)` (legacy `PDF_SOURCE_PATH` fallback when `root_id` is blank); `common.safe_join` delegates to the hardened `storage.safe_join`. See [.cursor/rules/storage.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/storage.mdc). Client op lists are re-validated server-side by `_sanitize_ops`.

## Routes (all `@login_required @admin_required`)

- `GET  /admin/toolbox` — tool landing (`admin_toolbox.html`).
- `GET  /admin/toolbox/pdf` — PDF Tool (`admin_toolbox_pdf.html`).
- `POST /pdf/upload` — multipart `pdf` OR `server_path` (+ optional `server_root`, `token`); stages one source, returns `{token, srcid, filename, page_count}`. The `pdf` field also accepts **image files** (`_IMAGE_EXTS`) — converted server-side to a one-page PDF at ~150 DPI (`_image_file_to_pdf`).
- `POST /pdf/add-pages` — `{token, srcid, mode, mode1_pages_per_student?, pre_rotate, dpi, filters}` → expands to descriptors (each tagged with `dpi`; Mode 1 pages also carry `mode1_pages_per_student`), appends, returns them.
- `POST /pdf/reorder` — `{token, order:[id]}`.
- `POST /pdf/page-ops` — `{token, page_id, ops}` replace one page's chain (sanitised).
- `POST /pdf/page-delete` — `{token, page_ids}`.
- `POST /pdf/duplicate` — `{token, page_ids, after_id?}` clone pages (new ids, same src/page/ops/dpi) inserted after `after_id` (or end). Powers copy/paste. Returns `{pages:[clones], order:[id]}`.
- `POST /pdf/set-pages` — `{token, pages:[{id, src, page, ops, mode, mode1_pages_per_student, dpi, annots}]}` **wholesale replace** the working set (validated against the session's sources; bad entries dropped; annots re-sanitised). Powers **Undo** — the client is authoritative for the working set, so restoring a snapshot is just an overwrite.
- `GET  /pdf/thumb/<token>/<page_id>.png?w=|?dpi=[&annots=0]` — working-set page thumbnail (ops + annots applied; `annots=0` = clean background for the Konva editor). `dpi=` (page-size independent) renders at full export resolution for the enlarged preview; `w=` is the small grid thumb.
- `GET  /pdf/src-thumb/<token>/<srcid>/<int:idx>.png?w=` — raw source page thumbnail.
- `GET /pdf/text-search` — **SSE** phrase search. Query: `token`, `page_ids` (csv), `engine` (`auto`/`digital`/`ocr`), `term` (repeated), `fuzzy`, `threshold`, `case_sensitive`, `parallel`. Streams `job` → per-page `progress`/`skip` (word extraction — the slow OCR step — fanned across `min(TOOLBOX_OCR_WORKERS, cpu_count, npages)` workers via `app.parallel.run_parallel` when `parallel=1`; completion order) → a single `results` event `{results:{page_id:[{rect,term}]}, engines, pages_scanned}` (cross-page `find_matches` runs once, in original page order, AFTER all pages are scanned so cross-page phrases still match) → `done`. SSE means long scanned PDFs never hit a gateway timeout. Cancel via the shared `POST /pdf/llm-detect-cancel` (jobs share `pdf_import.new_job`). Words cached under `words/<page_id>.json` keyed by a versioned engine/ops/dpi/auto-orient signature. `auto` = digital when mappable + text layer, else OCR. OCR is **rotation-aware**: a page whose upright pass reads poorly (too few **confident** words OR a low good/total ratio — a sideways scan still emits lots of low-confidence gibberish, so word COUNT is not the signal) is re-OCR'd at 90/180/270°; the orientation with the most confident words wins (`_good_word_count`, Tesseract OSD `_detect_osd_rotation` breaks ties; gated by `TOOLBOX_OCR_AUTO_ORIENT`). `extract_words_ocr`/`get_page_words` return `(words, display_rot)`: words stay in **reading-upright** space (tight boxes; line grouping + tight/loose margins act on the correct axes) and the route rotates only the final match rects back onto the displayed page via `rotate_rect_frac(rect, display_rot)` — matching a rotated page in display space directly would put the gap-bridging margin on the wrong axis and fatten the boxes.
- `GET  /pdf/llm-detect?token=&page_ids=&endpoint_id=&instruction=&parallel=` — **SSE** per-page LLM box detection (render page with ops → `llm_client.chat` with `ai_prompts.build_pdf_generic_system/user_text(instruction)` → `parse_generic_boxes` → fractional rects). `parallel=1` fans pages across `app.parallel.run_parallel` workers (cloud endpoints with `max_concurrency>1` only, same rule as `_ai_parallel`; page events arrive in completion order). Reuses `pdf_import.new_job` for cancellation (`POST /pdf/llm-detect-cancel` `{job_id}`). Gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`; endpoint list reuses `GET /admin/questions/ai/endpoints`, default endpoint `PDF_IMPORT_DEFAULT_LLM`.
- `POST /pdf/export` — `{token, page_ids?, fmt:'pdf'|'zip', split_every?, filename?, output:'digital'|'image', compress:'none'|'light'|'medium'|'strong'|'size', target_mb?}` → file download (`_parse_compress` maps the fields to the `pdf_tools` compress dict).
- `POST /pdf/export-save` (`-start`) — `{token, page_ids?, fmt, split_every?, filename, dest?, dest_root?, overwrite?, output, compress, target_mb?}` → saves under `<root>/<dest>` (`dest_root` resolved via `_resolve_root_base(require_write=True)`, legacy `PDF_SOURCE_PATH` when blank; `dest` rel folder, falls back to `TOOLBOX_SAVE_SUBDIR`). Filename is **required**. Existence is checked **before** building the bytes: if the target exists and `overwrite` is not set, returns **409** `{exists:true, filename, error}` so the client can prompt Overwrite/Rename. No silent auto-suffix.
- `POST /pdf/mkdir` — `{path, name, dest_root?}` create a sub-folder under `<root>/<path>` (writable root required; name sanitised to a single segment). Returns `{rel_path}`. (Now mostly handled inside the unified selector's own mkdir.)
- `POST /pdf/discard` — delete the staging dir.

Export is synchronous (no SSE) — fast enough for typical jobs.

## Frontend ([templates/admin_toolbox_pdf.html](mdc:templates/admin_toolbox_pdf.html))

Plain `fetch()` JSON + a client `pages[]` array (`{id, src, page, mode, dpi, baseOps, edit:{type→op}, nonce, annots:[]}`). `fullOps(p)` = `baseOps` + per-page `edit` ops in a fixed order; `nonce` cache-busts the thumb after edits.

- **Layout**: step 1 = upload only; step 2 = "Process & add" holds the **active-source page strip**, **Resolution (DPI)**, rotate/split, optional **deskew** only (no brightness/contrast/sharpen/grayscale/B&W — those are step 3); step 3 = preview/assemble + operations toolbar. **Desktop (≥992px) is app-like**: `.tb-left-col` and `.tb-right-col` are `position: sticky` below the navbar; the right card (`.tb-right-card`) is `height: calc(100vh - 76px)` flex-column with `#previewCanvas` as the internal scroll container (toolbar/export bar always visible); the left steps panel scrolls internally too. The rubber band tracks anchor/box/card hits entirely in the canvas's **content space** (client coords + scroll offsets) so pages scrolled out of view stay selected mid-drag, and auto-scrolls file-explorer-style when the pointer nears the top/bottom edge (48 px zone, speed scales with depth, rAF loop; falls back to window scroll on narrow layouts).
- **Selection model**: `selected` Set + `lastClickedId`. Click = single, Ctrl/Cmd-click = toggle, Shift-click = range (`selectRange`), rubber-band drag on the **canvas** background (`initRubberBand` listens on `#previewCanvas`, which wraps `#previewGrid` with a tall `min-height` + wide gaps so there's plenty of empty space to start a drag; rect-intersection; Shift/Ctrl = additive). **Select mode** (`setSelectMode`, toggled by `#selectModeBtn` or a ~500 ms **long-press** on a card via `beginLongPress`) makes every tap toggle selection (check overlays via `.tb-select-mode` body class), disables SortableJS while active, and shows "Done" on the button; Esc exits. Long-press timer is cancelled on pointer move / Sortable drag start.
- **Shared operations toolbar**: built once by `buildToolbars()` from `imageOpsHTML()` and injected into BOTH `#mainImageOps` (main, `.tb-needs-sel` auto-disabled when nothing selected) and `#modalImageOps` (enlarged preview, always enabled). Ops resolve their target via **`currentTargets()`** = `[currentPreviewPage]` when the modal is open, else `selectedPagesInOrder()` — so the same buttons work in both places. Rotate-L/R, a single **Adjust** dropdown (`[data-adjustmenu]` → `adjustMenuHTML`/`initAdjustMenus`: Brightness/Contrast/Sharpen sliders → `applyAdjust`, Grayscale/Deskew checks → `applyCheckToggle`, B&W check + 0–255 threshold → `applyBw`, "Reset adjustments" → `resetAdjusts`), **Mark up** (`openAnnotEditor`), **Find & Mark**, and **Reset**. Dropdowns populate from the first target on `show.bs.dropdown`, apply on `change`, use `data-bs-auto-close="outside"`. `saveMany` persists the **whole working set in one atomic `/set-pages` call** — NOT per-page `/page-ops` (concurrent `Promise.all` writes raced on `session.json`). Keyboard (`initKeyboard`, ignored while typing or while the annot editor is open — `tbAnnotEditorActive`): Del, Ctrl+A/C/X/V, **Ctrl+Z** (undo), Esc; when the modal is open arrows page prev/next instead.
- **Reorder ops**: a **Reorder** dropdown (`[data-reorder]` → `reorderOp(kind)`) rearranges the selection (≥2) or all pages. `arrangeIds(ids, kind)` for the 5 kinds: `interleave` (weave halves A0,B0,…), `deinterleave` (even-index group then odd-index group — inverse of interleave), `alt_interleave` (interleave with 2nd half reversed, for reversed duplex backs), `alt_deinterleave` (its inverse), `reverse`. Result placed back into the same positions, then `/reorder`.
- **Undo**: `undoStack` of `snapshotPages()` (deep clone of `{id,src,page,mode,dpi,baseOps,edit}`). `pushUndo()` is called **before** each mutation (add, edit, delete, paste, reorder-op, and on actual drag move). `doUndo()` pops, restores `pages` (bumps every `nonce` to refetch thumbs), intersects `selected`, and mirrors the snapshot to the server via `/set-pages` (`pushServerPages`). `#undoBtn` enabled iff the stack is non-empty.
- **Clipboard**: `copySel`/`cutSel` set `clipboard={mode,ids}`; `pasteClipboard` → copy uses `/duplicate` (inserts clones after the last selected), cut moves locally + `/reorder`. Cut pages get a `.tb-cut` style.
- **Reorder (drag)**: SortableJS on `.tb-page-card` (whole card draggable, `forceFallback`). `onStart` selects the dragged card if not already selected, snapshots for undo, and for a **multi-selection** collapses the other selected cards away (`.tb-drag-collapsing` → scale 0) and turns the `.sortable-fallback` drag image into a **stack** (`.tb-multi-drag` offset layers + a `.tb-drag-badge` count). `onEnd` moves the **whole selection** as a contiguous block to the drop point (computed from DOM anchor); only persists + pushes undo if the order actually changed; re-renders deferred via `setTimeout`.
- **Enlarged preview** (`#previewModal`): double-click a card → `openPreview`. **Quick / Full res** toggle (`setPreviewRes`, sticky module flag `previewRes` persisted as `localStorage.oqb_tbPreviewRes`, default thumb `?w=1100`; full = `/thumb?dpi=`, badge shows px dims), `prev/next` buttons + `stepPreview` (← / → keys, honours the sticky res) + on-image touch **tap zones** (`#modalTapPrev/Next`), and the shared modal toolbar (ops act on `currentPreviewPage`).
- **Annotation editor** ([templates/partials/pdf_annotate_editor.html](mdc:templates/partials/pdf_annotate_editor.html), included in `extra_js` after the main script — shares its globals): fullscreen Konva modal via `openAnnotEditor(pageId)`. Tools select/redact/erase("Remove")/highlight/text/pen (V/R/E/H/T/P), palette + custom colour (hidden for erase — always white), highlight-opacity + pen-width sliders, Transformer move/resize, **Copy to → all/selected pages**, per-page/global **Accept** + global **Discard** for pending marks, prev/next page (arrows), Quick/Full-res background (`?annots=0`), and an **Image** button (`#aeImageBtn` + hidden file input → `aeInsertImageFile`: canvas-downscale to ≤1400 px, PNG keeps alpha else JPEG 0.85, ≤4 MB data URL, placed at the viewport centre at 40% page width as a `kind:'image'` annot; Konva.Image nodes load via the `aeStampCache`). **Text tool is inline-Acrobat-style**: click page (or click/dbl-click an existing text mark) → positioned `#aeTextArea` overlay, type directly (Enter = newline, Ctrl+Enter/blur commit, Esc cancel); typeface (`#aeFont` Helvetica/Times/Courier ↔ `font` token) + size in pt (`#aeFontSize`, frac = pt/842 `AE_PT`) controls apply to the live editor / selection and set defaults — the textarea `blur` handler skips commit when `relatedTarget` is inside `#aeTextWrap`/`#aeColors`/`#aeCustomColor` and the control refocuses the textarea after applying, so restyling never kicks you out of edit mode. **Per-page undo/redo** (`aeHistory` Map of JSON stacks, `aeSnap()` before each mutation incl. dragstart/transformstart, Ctrl+Z/Y + header buttons; separate from the grid's global undo). **Zoom/pan**: stage-level scale+position (`aeSetZoom` 1–8×, wheel @pointer, pinch + two-finger pan, +/−/0 keys, header buttons, % = fit) — all drawing math reads `aeStage.getRelativePointerPosition()` so coords stay exact under zoom; pan = **right-drag** (context menu suppressed on the stage container) / middle-drag / space-drag / two-finger. Edits buffer in `aeAnnots`; on close → one `pushUndo` + atomic `/set-pages` + refresh of touched cards. Grid cards show ✏-count + pending-count badges (`editBadges`).
- **Find & Mark** (`#findMarkModal`): term rows (text + highlight/redact/**remove** kind + colour, colour input disabled for remove), scope (selected/all), engine **Auto / Digital / OCR / AI** (OCR disabled when Tesseract missing, AI when `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` off), fuzzy toggle + threshold, case toggle, and a shared **Run pages in parallel** checkbox (`#fmParallel`, hidden for the always-instant `digital` engine). AI engine has a **mode toggle** (`fmAiMode`): *Find the search terms* (terms keep their per-term styles) vs *Custom instruction* (own textarea + dedicated kind/colour style row — `opts.customStyle`, never the first term's style) + endpoint picker. **Both text and AI engines stream over SSE with live progress + a Stop button**: text → `runFindMarkText` (`EventSource` on `/text-search`, collects the `results` event), AI → `runFindMarkAI` (`/llm-detect`). Results become **pending** annots (`fmApplyResults` — one undo step) reviewed in grid/editor; modal footer offers **Accept all** / **Discard pending** (`fmSyncPendingButtons`).
- **Grid size slider** (`#gridSizeRange`, in the hint row above the canvas): sets the `--tb-card-w` CSS var consumed by `.tb-preview-grid`'s `minmax()`; persisted as `localStorage.oqb_tbGridW` (80–340 px, default 120).
- **Pickers use the unified selector** (`partials/file_selector.html`, `window.OQBFileSelector`): `pickServerBtn` → `OQBFileSelector.open({mode:'file', extensions:['.pdf']})` → `uploadSource(null, rel_path, root_id)`; `openSaveDest` → `OQBFileSelector.open({mode:'folder'})` → sets `saveDest`/`saveDestRoot` then `doSaveServer(false)` (body `dest` + `dest_root`). The old in-page server/dest modals + `loadDestDir`/`createFolder`/`loadServerDir` are gone.
- **Export**: file name is **required** (`updateExportButtons` disables both buttons when empty; defaults to the source PDF's name on first load) and **scope is confirmed**: with a partial selection, `resolveExportScope()` opens `#exportScopeModal` ("Selected only (N)" / "All pages"; dismiss = cancel) before download or the save-dest picker (chosen ids stick in `saveScopeIds` for overwrite retries). **Compression** select (`#exportCompress` none/light/medium/strong/size + `#exportTargetMb` MB input shown for size; hidden for ZIP-of-PNGs format) feeds `compress`/`target_mb` in the body. Buttons show a spinner via `setBtnLoading`. Save-to-server 409 → `#overwriteModal` (Overwrite re-POSTs with `overwrite:true`; Rename focuses the name field). "Separate file every N pages" shows only when the export scope has Mode-1 pages with one consistent `mode1_pages_per_student` value; mixed counts disable the shortcut.
- **Drag & drop import**: `initDropZone` on `#previewCanvas` — dropping PDF **or image** files uploads each (`uploadSource`) and adds all pages untouched via `addPagesWithDefaults` (mode `none`, no pre-rotate/filters, `DEFAULT_DPI`), skipping steps 1–2. `.tb-drop-hover` outlines the canvas during drag-over.
- **Crop tool**: toolbar `data-op="crop"` → `openCropModal(currentTargets())` (`#cropModal`): draw/move/resize a box on the first target's 1100-px thumb (pointer events, corner `.crop-handle`s), Apply writes `p.edit.crop = {type:'crop', box}` to **every** target. `fullOps` puts `crop` **last** in the edit order (the box is drawn on the fully-rendered page, so it applies in post-everything space); re-crop composes the new fractional box into the previous one; **Remove crop** deletes `edit.crop`. Crop+rotate combos still raster-fallback on export (existing rule); marks placed before a crop are NOT remapped (gotcha 5).

Server PDF picker reuses `admin.pdf_import_source_list` (`?path=` → `{configured, current_path, dirs, files}`).

## Config

`TOOLBOX_RASTER_WIDTH` (preview width, default 1700), `TOOLBOX_EXPORT_WIDTH` (legacy raster width fallback, default 2200), `TOOLBOX_DEFAULT_DPI` (processing/export DPI, default 200 — **registered in System Settings**, group "Toolbox"), `TOOLBOX_OCR_DPI` (Find & Mark OCR render DPI, default 300 — System Settings "Toolbox"), `TOOLBOX_OCR_WORKERS` (parallel Find & Mark workers, default 4, capped by cpu_count — System Settings "Toolbox"), `TOOLBOX_OCR_AUTO_ORIENT` (bool, default on — retry OCR at 90/180/270° on sparse pages — System Settings "Toolbox"), `TOOLBOX_SAVE_SUBDIR` (default `Saved`), `TESSERACT_CMD` (optional `.env`-only path to `tesseract.exe`; [app/pdf_text.py](mdc:app/pdf_text.py) auto-detects common install dirs + PATH when unset) — all in [app/config.py](mdc:app/config.py). Dependencies `pypdf>=4.0` (vector export; degrades to raster if absent), `rapidfuzz` (fuzzy match; falls back to exact), `pytesseract` + a local Tesseract install (OCR engine; UI option disabled when missing). Deskew needs NumPy (shared with `pdf_layout`); the deskew control is disabled when NumPy is missing.

## Batch PDF Import reuse

[app/pdf_import.py](mdc:app/pdf_import.py) `rasterize_pdf` / `stage` now call `pdf_tools` (`split_descriptors`, `build_op_chain`, `rasterize_page`, `apply_ops`) and accept `pre_rotate` / `split_mode` / `filters` (stored in `meta.json`). The legacy `deskew` flag is merged into `filters`. UI controls live in the **"Pre-process scans"** `<details>` in [templates/admin_pdf_import.html](mdc:templates/admin_pdf_import.html) (`ppRotate`/`ppSplit`/`ppBrightness`/`ppContrast`/`ppSharpen`/`ppGray`/`ppBw`/`ppBwThreshold` → form fields `pre_rotate`/`split_mode`/`f_*`). See [pdf-import.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/pdf-import.mdc).

## Gotchas

1. Vector crop on a page that already carries `/Rotate` is ambiguous in mediabox space → rasterise (handled in `_add_page`).
2. Heavy libs (`fitz`/`PIL`/`pypdf`) are imported lazily so importing `pdf_tools` never fails on a box missing one.
3. `rotate` deg is clockwise (negated for PIL's CCW positive angle) to match pypdf `/Rotate`.
4. Splitting in Batch PDF Import renumbers staged PNGs contiguously in final reading order; downstream page indices stay valid.
5. Annot coords live in **post-ops** space — rotating/cropping a page *after* marking it does NOT remap its annots. The digital-export mapper (`_fitz_annotated_page_bytes`) inverts rotate/crop into unrotated source space; geometry-warping raster ops (`deskew`, `rotate_fine`) force that page to raster and block the `digital` text-search engine (`pdf_text.GEOMETRY_BREAKERS`).
6. `pdf_text.find_matches` slides a fuzzy window over the **concatenated word stream of all searched pages**, so phrases wrapped across lines or page boundaries still match (boxes emitted per page/line). Match boxes use an asymmetric margin — horizontal ~25% of median word height (bridges inter-word gaps), vertical ~6% (hugs the line); `_group_lines` merges words into a line only when vertical centres are within 45% of line height.
